
Product Requirements Document (PRD): ISO 27001 AI-Certification Portal
Project Name: ISO 27001:2022 Lead Auditor 
Platform: ISO-Audit360.com
Version: 2026.1.0
1. Executive Summary
The goal is to launch an industry-first, free certification portal that uses Just-In-Time (JIT) AI Generation to provide unique, high-integrity exams for ISO 27001:2022. By enforcing a strict 15-second per-question limit, we shift the assessment from "memorization" to "audit-ready instinct," providing users with a "2026 Premium" digital credential.

2. Target Audience & Value Proposition
The User: GRC professionals, aspiring lead auditors, and ISMS consultants.
The Problem: Most free certifications are static, easily "Googleable," and lack professional prestige.
The Solution: An exam that is impossible to cheat on due to randomized AI generation and hard-locked timers, resulting in a highly-valued LinkedIn-ready certificate.

3. Comprehensive User Journey & Functional Specs
3.1 Landing & Acquisition (/iso-27001)
High-Fidelity UI: Dark-themed "Executive" aesthetic with gold accents.
Trust Indicators: Clear breakdown of the 10-minute/50-question protocol.
Call to Action: "Verify Identity & Start Audit."
3.2 Registration & Verification (Security Layer)
Fields: Full Name, Professional Email, Company, Role, Country.
OTP Logic: Mandatory email verification to prevent sybil/bot account creation.
Dashboard: Post-verification, the user lands on a "Readiness Dashboard" to choose between Associate (Clauses) or Professional (Annex A) tracks.


3.3 The AI-Generation Engine (The "Wait" Phase)
Upon the user selecting a track and clicking "Start Generation," the system initiates a 3-minute secure window. The backend identifies the track_id and triggers 5 parallel AI threads specifically tuned to that syllabus.
A. Associate Track: ISMS Foundation (Clauses focus)
Target: Mastery of the ISO 27001:2022 Management System framework.
Thread 1 (Core Context): 10 Qs on Clause 4 (Context) and Clause 5 (Leadership).
Thread 2 (Planning): 10 Qs on Clause 6 (Risk Assessment & Treatment).
Thread 3 (Resources): 10 Qs on Clause 7 (Competence & Awareness).
Thread 4 (Operations): 10 Qs on Clause 8 (Operational Planning & Control).
Thread 5 (Evaluation): 10 Qs on Clause 9 (Internal Audit) and Clause 10 (Improvement).
B. Professional Track: Lead Auditor (Annex A & 19011 focus)
Target: Practical application, control validation, and audit management.
Thread 1 (Organizational): 10 Qs on Annex A 5 (Organizational Controls).
Thread 2 (People & Physical): 10 Qs on Annex A 6 (People) and Annex A 7 (Physical).
Thread 3 (Technological): 10 Qs on Annex A 8 (Technological Controls).
Thread 4 (Scenario Auditing): 10 Qs on Identifying Non-Conformities (NCs) in case studies.
Thread 5 (Audit Governance): 10 Qs on ISO 19011 Principles (Opening meetings, evidence gathering, reporting).
C. Generation UX & "Audit Wisdom" Logic
To prevent user drop-off during the 3-minute generation, the UI will display a dynamic progress bar paired with track-specific content:
Associate Track Loaders: Show "Clause Reminders" (e.g., “Did you know? Clause 6.1.2 is where the risk identification process is defined.”)
Professional Track Loaders: Show "Auditor Ethics" (e.g., “A Lead Auditor must remain objective and evidence-based at all times.”)
D. Validation & "Start" Trigger
JSON Schema Check: Backend validates all 50 questions for correct format.
Uniqueness Check: System compares generated IDs against the user's last 3 attempts (Overlap Rule).
Active Start: Once validated, the "Generate" loader transforms into a High-Intensity "Enter Exam" Button, and the 10-minute global timer is prepped for the first user interaction.


3.4 The Exam Interface (The "Pressure-Cooker")
Dual-Timer Control:
Total Exam Timer: 600s (10:00 mins) constant countdown.
Per-Question Timer: 15s countdown.
Non-Reversibility: Selecting an option immediately locks it. If the 15s expires, the server logs a "Fail" for that question and auto-pushes the next.
Server-Side Sync: State is saved every 5 seconds to prevent loss during network flickers; however, the clock never pauses.

Future scope: The "Audit Simulation" Case Study Module


4. Result Analytics & Certification
4.1 The "Audit Report" (Feedback Loop)
Pass Threshold: 40/50 (80%).
Gap Analysis: A radar chart visualizing performance across the 5 domains mentioned in Section 3.3.
Corrective Actions: Lists incorrect answers with AI-generated explanations citing specific ISO 27001:2022 clauses.
4.2 Certificate Issuance (.jpeg Generation)
Format: 1920x1080 (Landscape) and 1080x1080 (Social Square).
Features: Unique ID (TPRM-2026-XXXX), "2026 Premium" gold seal, and QR code for instant verification.
Social Integration: Native LinkedIn/X sharing buttons with pre-filled hashtags.

5. Technical Requirements & Security
Stack: Next.js (Frontend), Fastify/Node.js (Backend), Redis (Timer State), Sharp (Image Rendering).
Anti-Cheat: * Disabled right-click/copy-paste.
Tab-focus monitoring (Automated submission if user leaves the tab > 3 times).
AI-generated distractors (wrong options) designed to mimic common auditor mistakes.

6. Success Metrics (KPIs)
Lead Generation: Registration-to-Verified Email ratio (>85%).
Viral Coefficient: % of users who share their certificate on LinkedIn.
Integrity Score: Average time taken per question (aiming for 8-12 seconds).
Content Quality: User-reported accuracy of AI-generated questions.



